CLAIM 17: Lessons / memory injection

GOAL: Verify completed runs can create scoped lessons and later worker prompts include them.

== STATIC CODE EVIDENCE ==

Lesson schema and storage:
- src/goal/lessons.ts:25 `LESSONS_FILENAME = "goal-lessons.json"` — single JSON file under the
  resolved state directory.
- src/goal/lessons.ts:35 `LESSON_SOURCES = new Set(["ralph","autocheck","user_edit","feedback","worker"])`
- src/goal/lessons.ts:36 `LESSON_SCOPES = new Set(["global","project"])`
- src/goal/lessons.ts:42-52 `Lesson` type: id, workingDir, pattern, lesson, source, scope?, runId,
  stepId?, createdAt.
- src/goal/lessons.ts:66 `resolveLessonsPath(stateDir = resolveStateDir())` — state-dir aware so
  the active MOLTBOT_STATE_DIR is honoured (matches the verified runtime convention used in
  claims 1/3/6).
- src/goal/lessons.ts:74-83 `atomicWriteJson` — temp + rename + chmod 0o600.
- src/goal/lessons.ts:127-153 `acquireLessonsWriteLock` — mkdir-based mutex with a 5s deadline,
  guarding concurrent writers (single mutation path / lessons.ts:163-171).

Writing scoped lessons:
- src/goal/lessons.ts:155 `export function addLesson(lesson)` — assigns id+createdAt, defaults
  `scope` to "project" when omitted, persists under lock.
- src/goal/lessons.ts:581 `export async function extractRunLessons(runId, workingDir, existingLessons)`
  — entry point invoked after a completed run; loads the run via loadRun (lessons.ts:587),
  builds a correction summary from plan history + ralph insights + step results
  (lessons.ts:456-522), returns [] early if `hasCorrections` is false (lessons.ts:590-591),
  asks the local Claude Code CLI first (lessons.ts:601-612) then Codex (lessons.ts:614-622)
  to emit `{lessons:[...]}` candidates, and finally records each candidate by calling
  `addLesson(... source:"autocheck", scope: candidate.scope ...)` (lessons.ts:629-637).
- src/goal/lessons.ts:538-579 `buildLessonExtractionPrompt` — explicit prompt rules pin scope
  classification to `global` or `project`, require kebab-case patterns, and reject lessons
  that merely restate fixes already visible in source (this is the contract that makes
  "scoped lessons" defensible in the README).

Reading lessons for the active worker:
- src/goal/lessons.ts:174-180 `export function getLessonsForContext(workingDir)` — returns all
  global-scope lessons plus project-scope lessons whose `workingDir` matches the active
  working directory.

Injecting lessons into the next worker prompt:
- src/goal/cli-runner.ts:7  `import { getLessonsForContext } from "./lessons.js";`
- src/goal/cli-runner.ts:33-36 `const lessons = getLessonsForContext(context.workingDir).map(...)`
  — collapses each Lesson to `{pattern, lesson}` and passes them into the CLI worker call.
- src/goal/cli-runner.ts:52 `lessons,` — argument is forwarded to `executeTaskWithCliWorker`.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:48 worker `executeTaskWithCliWorker` accepts `lessons?: Array<{pattern,lesson}>`.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:224, 258 lessons are propagated through the worker bootstrap chain.
- src/goal/cli-worker.ts:540-582 `export function buildCliWorkerPrompt(...)` — the prompt
  builder. When `lessons.length > 0` (cli-worker.ts:576-582) it writes a literal block:
      LESSONS FROM PRIOR RUNS (knowledge from previous work in this project):
      - [<pattern>]: <lesson>
      ...
  into the prompt that is handed to the local CLI worker (Codex / Claude Code).

Note that this exact "LESSONS FROM PRIOR RUNS" block is observable in the prompt this very
worker received — a direct end-to-end demonstration that the injection path is wired.

== INTERPRETATION ==

- Completed runs CAN produce scoped lessons: `extractRunLessons` is the documented entry
  point, candidates are tagged with `scope: "global" | "project"` per the prompt contract,
  and each survives an explicit shape check before being written via `addLesson`.
- Later worker prompts DO include them: `getLessonsForContext(workingDir)` filters by scope
  + working directory, the CLI runner attaches them to the worker invocation, and the prompt
  builder emits a labelled section that is delivered verbatim to the local CLI worker.

== SAFE README WORDING ==

OK to say: "Completed runs can extract scoped lessons; lessons tagged `project` are scoped to
the working directory they were learned in, lessons tagged `global` apply everywhere."
OK to say: "Before a worker starts a step, prior lessons for the active working directory are
injected into the worker prompt under a labelled section."

== UNSAFE WORDING TO AVOID ==

Avoid: "Long-term memory" / "the agent remembers everything across runs" — only extracted
lessons (kebab-pattern + 1-3 sentence text) are persisted, not full transcripts.
Avoid: "Automatic learning" — lesson extraction depends on a local Claude Code or Codex CLI
being available (lessons.ts:601-622); if neither is, no lessons are written.
Avoid: claiming lessons are shared across machines — they live in the local state dir.

STATUS: verified
REASON: Writers (addLesson at src/goal/lessons.ts:155; extractRunLessons at
